      "text": "Charles Grandison Finney served as the president of Oberlin College from 1851 to 1866, during which he was influential in the college's abolitionist activities.",
      "date": "1851"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Oberlin-Wellington Rescue",
      "text": "In 1858, Oberlin College was involved in the Oberlin-Wellington Rescue, a notable event in the abolitionist movement where students and faculty helped rescue a fugitive slave.",
      "date": "1858"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Black Graduate",
      "text": "In 1844, George B. Vashon became the first African American graduate of Oberlin College.",
      "date": "1844"
