      "date": "1942-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Development",
      "text": "After World War II, Port Moresby underwent significant development and expansion, becoming the capital of the Territory of Papua and New Guinea, and later the independent nation of Papua New Guinea in 1975.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence of Papua New Guinea",
      "text": "On September 16, 1975, Papua New Guinea gained independence from Australia, and Port Moresby became the capital of the newly independent country.",
