      "headline": "Return to Vienna",
      "text": "Schoenberg returned to Vienna in 1903, where he continued to compose and teach.",
      "date": "1903"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Atonality",
      "text": "Around 1908, Schoenberg began developing his atonal style, which abandoned traditional tonal harmony.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Invention of the Twelve-Tone Technique",
      "text": "In 1921, Schoenberg developed the twelve-tone technique, a method of composition using a series of all twelve notes in the chromatic scale.",
      "date": "1921"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Emigration to the United States",
      "text": "In 1933, due to the rise of the Nazi regime, Schoenberg emigrated to the United States, where he continued his work as a composer and teacher.",
      "date": "1933"
