      "text": "In settlements situated in the upper Euphrates area, Dagon was regarded as the 'father of gods', similar to Mesopotamian Enlil or Hurrian Kumarbi. He was also seen as a lord of the land, a god of prosperity, and a source of royal legitimacy.",
      "date": "-03000"
