      "text": "In the 1960s, linguist William Stokoe published research recognizing ASL as a legitimate language with its own grammar and syntax, distinct from English.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ASL as a Lingua Franca",
      "text": "ASL has become widely learned as a second language and serves as a lingua franca among deaf communities in North America and other regions.",
      "date": "1960s"
    },
