      "headline": "Burial of Tutankhamun",
      "text": "Tutankhamun was buried in tomb KV62 in the Valley of the Kings. His burial included a variety of funerary objects and personal possessions, densely packed due to the limited space. This event took place shortly after his death, around 1323 BCE.",
      "date": "-01323"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Robberies of the Tomb",
      "text": "The tomb was entered by robbers twice in the years immediately following Tutankhamun's burial. Despite these intrusions, the mummy and most of the burial goods remained intact.",
      "date": "-01323"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rediscovery of the Tomb",
      "text": "The tomb of Tutankhamun was rediscovered by Howard Carter on November 4, 1922. Its entrance had been hidden by debris, which preserved its contents from being stripped during the Third Intermediate Period.",
      "date": "1922-11-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Opening of the Burial Chamber",
      "text": "On February 16, 1923, Howard Carter and his team opened the burial chamber of Tutankhamun, revealing the sarcophagus and the treasures within.",
      "date": "1923-02-16"
    }
  ]
}

