      "headline": "Dreyfus Promoted to Captain",
      "text": "In 1889, Alfred Dreyfus was promoted to the rank of captain in the French Army.",
      "date": "1889"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Affair Begins",
      "text": "In 1894, Alfred Dreyfus was wrongfully accused of espionage for Germany, marking the beginning of the Dreyfus Affair.",
      "date": "1894"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Convicted",
      "text": "On December 22, 1894, Alfred Dreyfus was convicted of treason by a military court and sentenced to life imprisonment on Devil's Island.",
      "date": "1894-12-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Degradation Ceremony",
      "text": "On January 5, 1895, Alfred Dreyfus was publicly degraded in a humiliating ceremony at the École Militaire in Paris.",
      "date": "1895-01-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Sent to Devil's Island",
      "text": "In 1895, Alfred Dreyfus was deported to Devil's Island, a penal colony off the coast of French Guiana.",
      "date": "1895"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Émile Zola's J'Accuse...!",
      "text": "On January 13, 1898, Émile Zola published an open letter titled 'J'Accuse...!' in the newspaper L'Aurore, accusing the French government of antisemitism and wrongful imprisonment of Dreyfus.",
      "date": "1898-01-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus's Second Trial",
      "text": "In 1899, Alfred Dreyfus was brought back to France for a second trial, where he was again found guilty but with extenuating circumstances.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Pardoned",
      "text": "On September 19, 1899, Alfred Dreyfus was pardoned by French President Émile Loubet, though his conviction was not overturned.",
      "date": "1899-09-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus's Conviction Annulled",
      "text": "On July 12, 1906, the French Supreme Court annulled Alfred Dreyfus's conviction, fully exonerating him.",
      "date": "1906-07-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Reinstated in the Army",
      "text": "In 1906, following his exoneration, Alfred Dreyfus was reinstated in the French Army and promoted to the rank of major.",
      "date": "1906"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Retires from the Army",
      "text": "In 1907, Alfred Dreyfus retired from the French Army.",
      "date": "1907"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dreyfus Participates in World War I",
      "text": "During World War I, Alfred Dreyfus served in the French Army, contributing to the war effort.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Alfred Dreyfus",
      "text": "Alfred Dreyfus died on July 12, 1935, in Paris, France.",
      "date": "1935-07-12"
    }
