      "date": "1974-10-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Dressed to Kill'",
      "text": "On March 19, 1975, Kiss released their third studio album, 'Dressed to Kill', which included the iconic track 'Rock and Roll All Nite'.",
      "date": "1975-03-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Breakthrough with 'Alive!'",
      "text": "Kiss released their first live album, 'Alive!', on September 10, 1975. The album was a commercial success and helped establish the band's reputation.",
      "date": "1975-09-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Destroyer'",
      "text": "On March 15, 1976, Kiss released 'Destroyer', their fourth studio album, which included hits like 'Detroit Rock City' and 'Beth'.",
      "date": "1976-03-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Departure of Peter Criss",
      "text": "Drummer Peter Criss left Kiss in 1980, marking the end of the band's original lineup.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Creatures of the Night'",
      "text": "Kiss released 'Creatures of the Night' on October 13, 1982. This was the band's tenth studio album and marked a return to their hard rock roots.",
      "date": "1982-10-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unmasking on MTV",
      "text": "Kiss appeared on MTV on September 18, 1983, without their iconic makeup for the first time, marking a new era for the band.",
      "date": "1983-09-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reunion Tour with Original Lineup",
      "text": "In 1996, Kiss reunited with the original lineup of Gene Simmons, Paul Stanley, Ace Frehley, and Peter Criss for a highly successful reunion tour.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Psycho Circus'",
      "text": "Kiss released 'Psycho Circus' on September 22, 1998. This was the first album with the original lineup since 1979's 'Dynasty'.",
