      "headline": "Ottoman Influence",
      "text": "By the 16th century, Circassia came under the influence of the Ottoman Empire, although it retained a degree of autonomy.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russo-Circassian War Begins",
      "text": "The Russo-Circassian War began in 1763 as the Russian Empire sought to expand its territory into the Caucasus region, including Circassia.",
      "date": "1763"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Circassian Genocide",
      "text": "The war culminated in the Circassian genocide, where approximately 99.5-99.8% of the Circassian population was either exiled or massacred by the Russian Empire. This tragic event marked the end of Circassian independence.",
      "date": "1864"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by the Russian Empire",
      "text": "Following the Russo-Circassian War, Circassia was officially annexed by the Russian Empire, and its territory was incorporated into the Russian administrative framework.",
