      "headline": "Introduction of RS-232",
      "text": "RS-232 was originally introduced in 1960 as a standard for serial communication transmission of data. It was designed to define the signals connecting between a Data Terminal Equipment (DTE) such as a computer terminal or PC, and a Data Circuit-terminating Equipment (DCE), such as a modem.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
