      "headline": "Charlemagne Crowned Emperor",
      "text": "On December 25, 800, Charlemagne was crowned as the first Emperor of the Romans in the West in over three centuries, marking the peak of the Carolingian dynasty.",
      "date": "0800-12-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Charlemagne",
      "text": "Charlemagne died in 814, which began an extended period of fragmentation of the Carolingian Empire.",
      "date": "0814"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of the Carolingian Empire",
      "text": "Following Charlemagne's death, the Carolingian Empire began to fragment and decline, eventually leading to the evolution of the Kingdom of France and the Holy Roman Empire.",
      "date": "0814"
    }
  ]
}

