    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of CDN Services",
      "text": "Throughout the early 2000s, various companies began offering CDN services, expanding the reach and capabilities of CDNs to include web objects, downloadable objects, applications, live streaming media, on-demand streaming media, and social media sites.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of CDN Market",
      "text": "By the mid-2000s, the CDN market expanded significantly with the entry of new players and the development of more advanced technologies to improve content delivery and performance.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CDNs and Cloud Integration",
      "text": "In the 2010s, CDNs began integrating with cloud services, enhancing their capabilities to provide scalable and efficient content delivery solutions.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CDNs in the Modern Internet",
      "text": "By the 2020s, CDNs have become a critical component of the modern Internet infrastructure, serving a large portion of Internet content and ensuring high availability and performance for users worldwide.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

