      "headline": "Birth of Marcel Duchamp",
      "text": "Henri-Robert-Marcel Duchamp was born on July 28, 1887, in Blainville-Crevon, France.",
      "date": "1887-07-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Major Artwork: Nude Descending a Staircase, No. 2",
      "text": "In 1912, Duchamp created 'Nude Descending a Staircase, No. 2', which became one of his most famous works and was exhibited at the Armory Show in New York in 1913.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of 'The Bride Stripped Bare by Her Bachelors, Even'",
      "text": "Between 1915 and 1923, Duchamp worked on 'The Bride Stripped Bare by Her Bachelors, Even', also known as 'The Large Glass'.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Readymade",
      "text": "In 1917, Duchamp submitted 'Fountain', a urinal signed 'R. Mutt', to the Society of Independent Artists exhibition, introducing the concept of the 'readymade'.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to the United States",
      "text": "Duchamp moved to the United States in 1915, where he became a central figure in the Dada movement.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Retirement from Art",
      "text": "In 1923, Duchamp declared that he was retiring from art to devote himself to chess.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of 'Étant donnés'",
      "text": "Between 1946 and 1966, Duchamp secretly worked on 'Étant donnés', a major assemblage that was revealed after his death.",
      "date": "1946"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Marcel Duchamp",
      "text": "Marcel Duchamp died on October 2, 1968, in Neuilly-sur-Seine, France.",
      "date": "1968-10-02"
    }
  ]
}

