      "headline": "March on Rome",
      "text": "The March on Rome was a mass demonstration in October 1922 that resulted in Benito Mussolini's National Fascist Party ascending to power in Italy. Mussolini was appointed Prime Minister on October 31, 1922.",
      "date": "1922-10-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Acerbo Law Passed",
      "text": "In July 1923, the Italian Parliament passed the Acerbo Law, which granted two-thirds of the seats in Parliament to the party with the largest number of votes, effectively solidifying Fascist control.",
      "date": "1923-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mussolini's Dictatorship Established",
      "text": "On January 3, 1925, Mussolini declared himself dictator of Italy, marking the beginning of his totalitarian regime.",
      "date": "1925-01-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lateran Treaty Signed",
      "text": "On February 11, 1929, the Lateran Treaty was signed between the Kingdom of Italy and the Holy See, recognizing Vatican City as an independent state and resolving the 'Roman Question.'",
      "date": "1929-02-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Invasion of Ethiopia",
      "text": "Italy invaded Ethiopia on October 3, 1935, leading to the Second Italo-Ethiopian War. This was part of Mussolini's expansionist policy.",
      "date": "1935-10-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Italy Joins Axis Powers",
      "text": "On May 22, 1939, Italy signed the Pact of Steel with Nazi Germany, formally aligning itself with the Axis Powers.",
      "date": "1939-05-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Italy Enters World War II",
      "text": "Italy entered World War II on June 10, 1940, by declaring war on France and the United Kingdom.",
      "date": "1940-06-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fall of Mussolini",
      "text": "On July 25, 1943, Mussolini was deposed and arrested following a vote of no confidence by the Grand Council of Fascism.",
      "date": "1943-07-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Armistice of Cassibile",
      "text": "On September 3, 1943, the Armistice of Cassibile was signed, and it was publicly announced on September 8, 1943, marking Italy's surrender to the Allies.",
      "date": "1943-09-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Fascist Italy",
      "text": "The Kingdom of Italy officially ended its fascist regime in 1943, transitioning to a co-belligerent status with the Allies against the Axis Powers.",
      "date": "1943"
    }
  ]
}

