      "headline": "Formation of the Third Coalition",
      "text": "In 1805, the Third Coalition was formed as an alliance between the United Kingdom, the Austrian Empire, the Russian Empire, Naples, Sicily, and Sweden to oppose Napoleon's France.",
      "date": "1805"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Trafalgar",
      "text": "On October 21, 1805, the British Royal Navy, under Admiral Lord Nelson, defeated the combined fleets of France and Spain at the Battle of Trafalgar, securing British naval supremacy.",
      "date": "1805-10-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Ulm",
      "text": "From October 15 to October 20, 1805, Napoleon's forces encircled and captured an Austrian army at the Battle of Ulm, leading to a decisive French victory.",
      "date": "1805-10-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Occupation of Vienna",
      "text": "On November 13, 1805, French forces occupied Vienna, the capital of the Austrian Empire, without significant resistance.",
      "date": "1805-11-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Austerlitz",
      "text": "On December 2, 1805, Napoleon achieved a decisive victory against the Russian and Austrian armies at the Battle of Austerlitz, also known as the Battle of the Three Emperors.",
      "date": "1805-12-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Pressburg",
      "text": "On December 26, 1805, the Treaty of Pressburg was signed, ending the War of the Third Coalition. Austria ceded territory to France and its allies, and recognized Napoleon's gains.",
      "date": "1805-12-26"
    }
  ]
}

