      "headline": "Marriage to Dora Kellner",
      "text": "Walter Benjamin married Dora Kellner in 1917, and they had a son, Stefan Rafael Benjamin, born in 1918.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Separation from Dora Kellner",
      "text": "Benjamin and Dora Kellner separated in 1930, although they never officially divorced.",
      "date": "1930"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Association with the Frankfurt School",
      "text": "In the late 1920s, Benjamin became associated with the Frankfurt School, a group of intellectuals known for their critical theory.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Friendship with Bertolt Brecht",
      "text": "During the 1930s, Benjamin developed a significant friendship with playwright Bertolt Brecht, which influenced his work.",
      "date": "1930"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fleeing Nazi Germany",
      "text": "In 1933, with the rise of the Nazi regime, Benjamin fled Germany and eventually settled in Paris, France.",
