      "headline": "Launch of Voyager 2",
      "text": "Voyager 2 was launched on August 20, 1977, from Cape Canaveral, Florida, aboard a Titan IIIE rocket. It was the first of the two Voyager spacecraft to be launched.",
      "date": "1977-08-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of Voyager 1",
      "text": "Voyager 1 was launched on September 5, 1977, from Cape Canaveral, Florida, aboard a Titan IIIE rocket. It was launched after Voyager 2 but followed a faster trajectory.",
      "date": "1977-09-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 1 Flyby of Jupiter",
      "text": "Voyager 1 made its closest approach to Jupiter on March 5, 1979, providing detailed images and data about the planet and its moons.",
      "date": "1979-03-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 2 Flyby of Jupiter",
      "text": "Voyager 2 made its closest approach to Jupiter on July 9, 1979, following its sister spacecraft and providing additional data and images.",
      "date": "1979-07-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 1 Flyby of Saturn",
      "text": "Voyager 1 made its closest approach to Saturn on November 12, 1980, capturing detailed images and data of the planet and its rings.",
      "date": "1980-11-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 2 Flyby of Saturn",
      "text": "Voyager 2 made its closest approach to Saturn on August 26, 1981, continuing its mission to explore the outer planets.",
      "date": "1981-08-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 2 Flyby of Uranus",
      "text": "Voyager 2 made its closest approach to Uranus on January 24, 1986, becoming the first spacecraft to visit the planet and providing valuable data.",
      "date": "1986-01-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 2 Flyby of Neptune",
      "text": "Voyager 2 made its closest approach to Neptune on August 25, 1989, completing its Grand Tour of the outer planets.",
      "date": "1989-08-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Voyager 1 Enters Interstellar Space",
      "text": "On August 25, 2012, Voyager 1 became the first human-made object to enter interstellar space, providing data about the heliosphere's boundary.",
