    {
      "headline": "Birth of Amir Khusrau",
      "text": "Amir Khusrau was born in 1253 in Patiyali, in present-day Uttar Pradesh, India. He was born into a family with a rich cultural and intellectual heritage.",
      "date": "1253"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service under Sultan Balban",
      "text": "In 1271, Amir Khusrau entered the service of Sultan Balban's nephew, Malik Chhajju, and began his career as a court poet.",
      "date": "1271"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service under Sultan Kaiqubad",
      "text": "In 1287, Khusrau entered the service of Sultan Kaiqubad, the grandson of Balban, and continued to gain fame as a poet and musician.",
      "date": "1287"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service under Sultan Jalaluddin Khalji",
      "text": "In 1290, Khusrau began serving Sultan Jalaluddin Khalji, the founder of the Khalji dynasty, and composed several works during this period.",
      "date": "1290"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service under Sultan Alauddin Khalji",
      "text": "In 1296, Khusrau entered the service of Sultan Alauddin Khalji, under whom he wrote some of his most famous works, including the 'Khamsa'.",
      "date": "1296"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the 'Khamsa'",
      "text": "In 1298, Amir Khusrau completed his famous work 'Khamsa', a collection of five epic poems inspired by the Persian poet Nizami.",
      "date": "1298"
