      "headline": "Social Security Act Signed into Law",
      "text": "On August 14, 1935, President Franklin D. Roosevelt signed the Social Security Act into law, establishing a system of old-age benefits for workers, benefits for victims of industrial accidents, unemployment insurance, aid for dependent mothers and children, the blind, and the physically handicapped.",
      "date": "1935-08-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Social Security Taxes Collected",
      "text": "In January 1937, the first Social Security taxes were collected, marking the beginning of the funding mechanism for the Social Security program.",
      "date": "1937-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Social Security Benefits Paid",
      "text": "On January 31, 1940, the first monthly retirement check was issued to Ida May Fuller of Ludlow, Vermont, for $22.54.",
      "date": "1940-01-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Social Security Amendments of 1956",
      "text": "In 1956, the Social Security Act was amended to include disability insurance benefits, expanding the scope of the program to cover disabled workers.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Medicare and Medicaid Established",
      "text": "On July 30, 1965, President Lyndon B. Johnson signed the Social Security Amendments of 1965 into law, which established Medicare and Medicaid, providing health insurance to the elderly and low-income individuals.",
      "date": "1965-07-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Social Security Amendments of 1972",
      "text": "The 1972 amendments introduced automatic cost-of-living adjustments (COLAs) to Social Security benefits, ensuring that benefits would keep pace with inflation.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Social Security Amendments of 1983",
      "text": "In 1983, major amendments were made to the Social Security Act to address funding issues, including gradually increasing the retirement age and taxing Social Security benefits for higher-income beneficiaries.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Social Security Administration Becomes Independent Agency",
      "text": "On March 31, 1995, the Social Security Administration became an independent agency, separating from the Department of Health and Human Services.",
      "date": "1995-03-31"
    }
  ]
}

