      "headline": "Expulsion from Egypt",
      "text": "According to the Hebrew Bible, the Israelites were enslaved in Egypt and later led out by Moses in an event known as the Exodus. This is traditionally dated to around the 13th century BCE.",
      "date": "-1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Babylonian Exile",
      "text": "In 586 BCE, the Babylonians conquered Jerusalem and destroyed the First Temple, leading to the exile of the Jewish population to Babylon.",
      "date": "-0586"
