      "headline": "Pogroms in the Russian Empire",
      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, waves of pogroms in the Russian Empire led to mass emigration of Jews, particularly to the United States and Palestine.",
      "date": "1881"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Holocaust and World War II",
      "text": "During World War II, the Holocaust led to the genocide of six million Jews and the displacement of millions more across Europe.",
      "date": "1941"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jewish Exodus from Arab and Muslim Countries",
      "text": "Between 1948 and the early 1970s, approximately 850,000 Jews were expelled or fled from Arab and Muslim countries, largely due to rising anti-Semitic sentiment and violence.",
      "date": "1948"
    }
