      "text": "By 28 November 1989, the Communist Party of Czechoslovakia announced it would relinquish power and dismantle the one-party state, marking the end of 41 years of Communist rule.",
      "date": "1989-11-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of New Government",
      "text": "On 10 December 1989, President Gustáv Husák appointed the first largely non-Communist government in Czechoslovakia since 1948, led by Prime Minister Marián Čalfa.",
