      "headline": "Compilation of the Talmud",
      "text": "The Talmud, consisting of the Mishnah and the Gemara, was completed around 500 CE. It serves as a central text of Rabbinic Judaism and a primary source of Halakha.",
      "date": "0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Codification by Maimonides",
      "text": "In 1177, Maimonides completed the Mishneh Torah, a comprehensive code of Jewish law that organized and clarified Halakha.",
      "date": "1177"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of the Shulchan Aruch",
      "text": "In 1563, Rabbi Joseph Karo published the Shulchan Aruch, a codification of Jewish law that became widely accepted as the authoritative legal code in Jewish communities.",
