      "text": "The National Liberation Army (ELN), another significant guerrilla group, was founded in 1964, contributing to the ongoing conflict.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise of Drug Trafficking",
      "text": "During the 1970s, drug trafficking became a significant factor in the Colombian conflict, with various groups engaging in the trade to fund their activities.",
      "date": "1970"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of Paramilitary Groups",
      "text": "In the 1980s, far-right paramilitary groups began to form, initially as self-defense forces against guerrilla groups, but later becoming involved in drug trafficking and human rights abuses.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Escobar's Influence",
      "text": "Pablo Escobar, a notorious drug lord, rose to power in the 1980s, significantly impacting the conflict through his control of the Medellín Cartel.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitutional Reform",
      "text": "In 1991, Colombia adopted a new constitution, aiming to address some of the social and political issues fueling the conflict.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Demobilization of Paramilitaries",
      "text": "In 2003, the Colombian government began a process to demobilize paramilitary groups, leading to the disbandment of the United Self-Defense Forces of Colombia (AUC) by 2006.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peace Talks with FARC",
      "text": "In 2012, the Colombian government initiated peace talks with FARC, aiming to end the decades-long conflict.",
      "date": "2012"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Peace Agreement with FARC",
      "text": "On November 24, 2016, the Colombian government and FARC signed a historic peace agreement, marking a significant step towards ending the conflict.",
      "date": "2016-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ongoing Violence",
      "text": "Despite the peace agreement with FARC, violence continues in Colombia due to the presence of other armed groups and criminal organizations.",
      "date": "2017"
    }
  ]
}

