      "text": "Operation Dragoon was initially designed to be executed in conjunction with Operation Overlord, the June 1944 Allied landing in Normandy. However, a lack of available resources led to a cancellation of the second landing.",
      "date": "1944-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reconsideration of Operation Dragoon",
      "text": "By July 1944, the landing was reconsidered due to the clogged-up ports in Normandy, which did not have the capacity to adequately supply the Allied forces. Concurrently, the high command of the French Liberation Army pushed for a revival of the operation that would include large numbers of French troops.",
      "date": "1944-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Approval of Operation Dragoon",
      "text": "The operation was finally approved in July 1944 to be executed in August.",
      "date": "1944-07"
    },
