      "text": "During World War I (1914-1918), nurses played a crucial role in caring for wounded soldiers, leading to increased recognition and professionalization of nursing.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nursing During World War II",
      "text": "World War II (1939-1945) saw a significant increase in the demand for nurses, leading to the establishment of the Cadet Nurse Corps in the United States to train more nurses.",
      "date": "1939"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Advanced Practice Nursing",
      "text": "In the mid-20th century, the role of advanced practice nurses, such as nurse practitioners and clinical nurse specialists, began to develop, expanding the scope of nursing practice.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the International Council of Nurses",
      "text": "The International Council of Nurses (ICN) was established in 1899, representing nurses worldwide and advocating for the profession.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nursing Shortages",
      "text": "Throughout the late 20th and early 21st centuries, many countries experienced significant nursing shortages, prompting efforts to recruit and retain more nurses.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
