      "text": "The League of Nations was established in 1920 as an international organization aimed at maintaining world peace and preventing future conflicts.",
      "date": "1920"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Economic Impact and Reparations",
      "text": "Germany was required to pay reparations to the Allied countries, which had significant economic impacts on the country and contributed to the hyperinflation of the 1920s.",
      "date": "1919"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Political Changes and Suffrage",
      "text": "World War I led to political transformations, with many countries, including Germany, Great Britain, and the United States, moving towards electoral democracies and near-universal suffrage.",
      "date": "1918-1920"
