      "headline": "Sampoong Department Store Collapse",
      "text": "On June 29, 1995, the Sampoong Department Store in Seoul, South Korea, collapsed due to a structural failure. The collapse killed 502 people and injured 937, making it the largest peacetime disaster in South Korean history.",
      "date": "1995-06-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction and Opening of Sampoong Department Store",
      "text": "The Sampoong Department Store was constructed and opened in 1989. It was a large, multi-story building located in the Seocho District of Seoul, South Korea.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Initial Structural Issues Identified",
      "text": "In 1994, cracks began to appear in the ceiling of the fifth floor of the Sampoong Department Store. Despite these warning signs, the building continued to operate.",
      "date": "1994"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Warning Signs Before Collapse",
      "text": "In the days leading up to the collapse, more cracks appeared, and the air conditioning units on the roof were moved, which added extra stress to the structure. These were ignored by the management.",
      "date": "1995-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Legal Consequences",
      "text": "Following the collapse, several executives and construction officials were arrested and charged. Lee Joon, the chairman of Sampoong Group, was sentenced to 10.5 years in prison for criminal negligence.",
      "date": "1995-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Memorial and Aftermath",
      "text": "A memorial was erected at the site of the collapse to honor the victims. The disaster led to significant changes in South Korean building regulations and safety standards.",
      "date": "1996"
    }
  ]
}

