      "headline": "Creation of Tabasco Sauce",
      "text": "In 1868, Edmund McIlhenny created the original Tabasco sauce on Avery Island, Louisiana. He used tabasco peppers, vinegar, and salt to develop the recipe.",
      "date": "1868"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Commercial Sales",
      "text": "In 1869, Tabasco sauce was first sold commercially. Edmund McIlhenny distributed the sauce in small cologne bottles, which were readily available and had a sprinkler fitment, making them ideal for dispensing the sauce.",
      "date": "1869"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Trademark Registration",
      "text": "In 1906, the McIlhenny Company registered the Tabasco trademark, ensuring the brand's protection and recognition.",
      "date": "1906"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of Pepper Cultivation",
      "text": "By the mid-20th century, the cultivation of tabasco peppers expanded beyond Avery Island to Central America, South America, and Africa to meet growing demand.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of New Varieties",
      "text": "Over the years, the McIlhenny Company introduced multiple varieties of Tabasco sauce, including habanero, chipotle, sriracha, and Trinidad Moruga scorpion.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Distribution",
      "text": "As of the 21st century, Tabasco products are sold in more than 195 countries and territories and are packaged in 36 languages and dialects.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
  ]
