      "text": "The American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) was founded on January 19, 1920, in response to the Palmer Raids and the Red Scare, which threatened civil liberties in the United States.",
      "date": "1920-01-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Major Case: Gitlow v. New York",
      "text": "In 1925, the ACLU was involved in its first major Supreme Court case, Gitlow v. New York, which helped establish the principle of applying the First Amendment to state governments.",
