      "headline": "Introduction of Strategic Bombers",
      "text": "The concept of strategic bombing emerged during World War I, with the development of aircraft capable of carrying large bomb loads over long distances to target enemy infrastructure and cities.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II and Strategic Bombing",
      "text": "During World War II, strategic bombing became a key military strategy. The United States and the United Kingdom conducted extensive bombing campaigns against Germany and Japan, using aircraft like the B-17 Flying Fortress and the B-29 Superfortress.",
      "date": "1939"
