      "headline": "First Mention of Potsdam",
      "text": "Potsdam was first mentioned in a document in 993 as a small settlement called 'Poztupimi'.",
      "date": "0993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Potsdam Receives Town Privileges",
      "text": "Potsdam was granted town privileges in 1345, marking its development as a recognized settlement.",
      "date": "1345"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Thirty Years' War Impact",
      "text": "During the Thirty Years' War (1618-1648), Potsdam suffered significant destruction and depopulation.",
      "date": "1618"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Frederick William's Development",
      "text": "In 1660, Frederick William, Elector of Brandenburg, began developing Potsdam as a garrison town.",
      "date": "1660"
