      "text": "In 272 AD, the Roman Emperor Aurelian recaptured Palmyra, ending Zenobia's rebellion and reasserting Roman control.",
      "date": "0272"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Destruction of Palmyra",
      "text": "In 273 AD, after another revolt, Aurelian destroyed Palmyra, significantly diminishing its importance and influence.",
      "date": "0273"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Byzantine and Islamic Periods",
      "text": "Palmyra was later part of the Byzantine Empire and then came under Islamic rule in the 7th century, experiencing various periods of decline and revival.",
      "date": "0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Rediscovery",
      "text": "In the 17th and 18th centuries, European travelers rediscovered Palmyra, leading to increased interest and archaeological exploration.",
      "date": "1700"
