      "text": "John Wycliffe was born around the year 1320 in the village of Hipswell, near Richmond in the North Riding of Yorkshire, England.",
      "date": "1320"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Education at Oxford",
      "text": "Wycliffe began his studies at the University of Oxford, where he would later become a prominent scholar and theologian.",
      "date": "1345"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Master of Balliol College",
      "text": "In 1361, Wycliffe became the Master of Balliol College, Oxford, marking his rise in academic and ecclesiastical circles.",
      "date": "1361"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rector of Fillingham",
      "text": "Wycliffe was appointed as the rector of Fillingham in Lincolnshire in 1361, a position he held while continuing his academic work.",
      "date": "1361"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rector of Ludgershall",
      "text": "In 1368, Wycliffe became the rector of Ludgershall, Buckinghamshire.",
      "date": "1368"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rector of Lutterworth",
      "text": "Wycliffe was appointed rector of Lutterworth in Leicestershire in 1374, a position he held until his death.",
      "date": "1374"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Involvement in Politics",
      "text": "Wycliffe became involved in politics, serving as a diplomat in negotiations between England and the Papacy in 1374.",
      "date": "1374"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Criticism of the Church",
      "text": "By the late 1370s, Wycliffe began to openly criticize the wealth and power of the Church, advocating for reform.",
      "date": "1378"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Translation of the Bible",
      "text": "Wycliffe is traditionally believed to have advocated for or been involved in the translation of the Bible into Middle English, completed around 1382.",
      "date": "1382"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Condemnation by the Church",
      "text": "In 1382, Wycliffe's teachings were condemned by the Church, and he was summoned to appear before a synod at Blackfriars, London.",
      "date": "1382"
    },
