      "headline": "Hugo Chávez Elected President",
      "text": "Hugo Chávez was elected President of Venezuela, marking the beginning of a new political era. His presidency laid the groundwork for future economic policies that would contribute to the crisis. Date: 1998.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chávez Implements Bolivarian Missions",
      "text": "In 2003, President Chávez implemented the Bolivarian Missions, a series of social programs aimed at reducing poverty. While initially successful, these programs later contributed to economic strain. Date: 2003.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Hugo Chávez",
      "text": "Hugo Chávez died on March 5, 2013, after a long battle with cancer. His death marked the end of his presidency and the beginning of Nicolás Maduro's leadership. Date: 2013-03-05.",
      "date": "2013-03-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nicolás Maduro Becomes President",
      "text": "Following Chávez's death, Nicolás Maduro was elected President of Venezuela. His presidency has been marked by economic decline and political unrest. Date: 2013.",
      "date": "2013"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Start of Hyperinflation",
      "text": "Venezuela began experiencing hyperinflation in 2014, with inflation rates rapidly increasing and severely impacting the economy. Date: 2014.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Massive Emigration Begins",
      "text": "Due to worsening economic conditions, massive emigration from Venezuela began around 2015, with millions of Venezuelans fleeing to neighboring countries. Date: 2015.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitutional Crisis",
      "text": "In 2017, Venezuela faced a constitutional crisis when the Supreme Court attempted to assume legislative powers, leading to widespread protests and international condemnation. Date: 2017.",
      "date": "2017"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Re-election of Nicolás Maduro",
      "text": "Nicolás Maduro was re-elected in May 2018 in a controversial election widely criticized for alleged irregularities and lack of transparency. Date: 2018-05.",
      "date": "2018-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Juan Guaidó Declares Interim Presidency",
      "text": "On January 23, 2019, Juan Guaidó, leader of the National Assembly, declared himself interim president, challenging Maduro's leadership and gaining international recognition. Date: 2019-01-23.",
      "date": "2019-01-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Blackout Crisis",
      "text": "In March 2019, Venezuela experienced a nationwide blackout, exacerbating the ongoing crisis and highlighting the country's infrastructure issues. Date: 2019-03.",
      "date": "2019-03"
    }
  ]
}

