    {
      "headline": "Origin of Mumblecore",
      "text": "The term 'mumblecore' was first coined by sound editor Eric Masunaga at the South by Southwest Film Festival in 2005 to describe a group of films characterized by naturalistic acting and dialogue, low budgets, and a focus on personal relationships.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Andrew Bujalski's 'Funny Ha Ha'",
      "text": "Andrew Bujalski's film 'Funny Ha Ha' is often considered one of the first mumblecore films. It was released in 2002 and set the tone for the genre with its focus on the personal relationships of young adults.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'The Puffy Chair'",
      "text": "In 2005, the Duplass brothers released 'The Puffy Chair', a film that became one of the defining works of the mumblecore genre, further popularizing its style and themes.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joe Swanberg's 'Hannah Takes the Stairs'",
      "text": "Released in 2007, Joe Swanberg's 'Hannah Takes the Stairs' is another key film in the mumblecore movement, featuring Greta Gerwig, who would become a prominent figure in the genre.",
      "date": "2007"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Greta Gerwig's Rise",
      "text": "Greta Gerwig emerged as a significant actress and filmmaker within the mumblecore genre, starring in several films including 'Hannah Takes the Stairs' and co-directing 'Nights and Weekends' in 2008.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Mumblegore",
      "text": "The term 'mumblegore' was introduced to describe films that blend mumblecore's naturalistic style with horror elements, with notable examples including 'Baghead' (2008) by the Duplass brothers.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lynn Shelton's 'Humpday'",
      "text": "Lynn Shelton's film 'Humpday', released in 2009, is another significant contribution to the mumblecore genre, exploring themes of friendship and sexuality.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mainstream Recognition",
      "text": "By the early 2010s, mumblecore had gained mainstream recognition, with filmmakers like the Duplass brothers transitioning to larger projects while maintaining the genre's influence.",
      "date": "2010"
    }
  ]
}

