      "headline": "University of Bologna Founded",
      "text": "The University of Bologna, considered the oldest university in the world, was founded in 1088. It became a center for legal studies and attracted students from across Europe.",
      "date": "1088"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Magna Carta Signed",
      "text": "In 1215, King John of England signed the Magna Carta, a charter of rights agreed to by the king and his barons. It is considered a foundational document in the development of modern democracy.",
      "date": "1215"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fourth Crusade",
      "text": "The Fourth Crusade, which took place from 1202 to 1204, was originally intended to conquer Muslim-controlled Jerusalem by means of an invasion through Egypt. Instead, the Crusaders sacked the Christian city of Constantinople.",
      "date": "1202"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Thomas Aquinas Born",
      "text": "Thomas Aquinas, a significant philosopher and theologian of the High Middle Ages, was born in 1225. His works, particularly the Summa Theologica, have had a lasting impact on Western thought.",
      "date": "1225"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the High Middle Ages",
      "text": "The High Middle Ages ended around the year 1300, transitioning into the Late Middle Ages. This period was characterized by significant social, political, and economic changes, including the Black Death and the Hundred Years' War.",
      "date": "1300"
    }
  ]
}

