      "text": "The term CAPTCHA was coined in 2000 by Luis von Ahn, Manuel Blum, Nicholas J. Hopper, and John Langford of Carnegie Mellon University. It stands for 'Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers and Humans Apart.'",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Use of CAPTCHA",
      "text": "The first use of CAPTCHA was implemented by Yahoo! to prevent bots from creating accounts on their platform.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "reCAPTCHA Development",
      "text": "In 2007, Luis von Ahn and his team developed reCAPTCHA, a more advanced version of CAPTCHA that helps digitize books by using words from scanned texts that OCR programs have difficulty recognizing.",
      "date": "2007"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Google Acquires reCAPTCHA",
      "text": "In 2009, Google acquired reCAPTCHA to help improve its book digitization efforts and enhance its security measures.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of No CAPTCHA reCAPTCHA",
      "text": "In 2014, Google introduced the No CAPTCHA reCAPTCHA, which simplified the user experience by allowing users to verify themselves with a single click, rather than deciphering distorted text.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of reCAPTCHA v3",
      "text": "In 2018, Google launched reCAPTCHA v3, which provides a frictionless user experience by assigning a risk score to each interaction, allowing site owners to take appropriate action.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
