      "headline": "Founding of Arc'teryx",
      "text": "Arc'teryx was founded in 1989 in North Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada. The company was originally named Rock Solid by founder Dave Lane.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rebranding to Arc'teryx",
      "text": "In 1991, the company rebranded from Rock Solid to Arc'teryx, inspired by the Archaeopteryx, a transitional fossil that represents the evolution from dinosaurs to birds.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Vapor Harness",
      "text": "In 1992, Arc'teryx introduced the Vapor Harness, a revolutionary climbing harness that utilized thermolamination technology.",
      "date": "1992"
