      "headline": "Foundation of the Kingdom of Pamplona",
      "text": "The Kingdom of Pamplona, later known as the Kingdom of Navarre, was established around the year 824. It was founded by Íñigo Arista, who became its first king.",
      "date": "0824"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Sancho III of Navarre",
      "text": "Sancho III, also known as Sancho the Great, reigned from 1004 to 1035. He expanded the kingdom significantly, bringing it to its greatest territorial extent.",
      "date": "1004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Division of the Kingdom",
      "text": "Upon the death of Sancho III in 1035, the kingdom was divided among his sons, leading to the creation of separate kingdoms including Castile, Aragon, and Navarre.",
      "date": "1035"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Union with Aragon",
      "text": "In 1076, the Kingdom of Navarre was united with the Kingdom of Aragon under King Sancho Ramírez after the assassination of King Sancho IV of Navarre.",
      "date": "1076"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence Restored",
      "text": "Navarre regained its independence in 1134 after the death of Alfonso I of Aragon, who died without an heir.",
      "date": "1134"
    },
    {
      "headline": "French Influence",
      "text": "In 1234, the French House of Champagne inherited the throne of Navarre, marking the beginning of significant French influence in the kingdom.",
      "date": "1234"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by Castile",
      "text": "In 1512, the southern part of Navarre was annexed by the Kingdom of Castile, effectively ending its independence in that region.",
      "date": "1512"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Union with France",
      "text": "In 1589, Henry III of Navarre became King Henry IV of France, uniting the crowns of Navarre and France.",
      "date": "1589"
    }
  ]
}

