      "headline": "Formation of the Derg",
      "text": "The Derg was formed in June 1974 as a committee of military officers to address grievances within the Ethiopian military and to oversee the transition of power from Emperor Haile Selassie.",
      "date": "1974-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Coup d'état and Overthrow of Emperor Haile Selassie",
      "text": "On September 12, 1974, the Derg led a coup d'état that deposed Emperor Haile Selassie, ending the Ethiopian monarchy and establishing a military government.",
      "date": "1974-09-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declaration of Ethiopia as a Socialist State",
      "text": "In December 1974, the Derg declared Ethiopia a socialist state, aligning itself with the Soviet Union and other communist countries.",
      "date": "1974-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Red Terror Campaign",
      "text": "From 1976 to 1978, the Derg conducted the Red Terror campaign, a violent political repression targeting opposition groups, resulting in thousands of deaths.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mengistu Haile Mariam Becomes Chairman",
      "text": "In February 1977, Mengistu Haile Mariam became the chairman of the Derg, consolidating power and becoming the de facto leader of Ethiopia.",
      "date": "1977-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ethiopian Civil War",
      "text": "The Ethiopian Civil War began in September 1974 and continued throughout the Derg's rule, with various rebel groups fighting against the government.",
      "date": "1974-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "1984–1985 Famine",
      "text": "A severe famine occurred in Ethiopia from 1984 to 1985, exacerbated by government policies and conflict, leading to international humanitarian efforts.",
      "date": "1984"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abolition of the Derg",
      "text": "In 1987, the Derg was formally dissolved and replaced by the People's Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, although Mengistu and his allies retained power.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Mengistu's Rule",
      "text": "Mengistu Haile Mariam fled Ethiopia in May 1991 as rebel forces closed in on Addis Ababa, marking the end of the Derg's influence.",
      "date": "1991-05"
    }
  ]
}

