      "headline": "Introduction to the New World",
      "text": "From France and Spain, the grape spread across Europe and to the New World, finding new homes in places like California's Napa Valley, New Zealand's Hawke's Bay, South Africa's Stellenbosch region, Australia's Margaret River, McLaren Vale and Coonawarra regions, and Chile's Maipo Valley and Colchagua.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Most Widely Planted Premium Red-Wine Grape",
      "text": "For most of the 20th century, Cabernet Sauvignon was the world's most widely planted premium red-wine grape.",
      "date": "1900"
