      "headline": "Introduction of Pluto in Greek Mythology",
      "text": "Pluto, also known as Ploutōn, was introduced in Greek mythology as the ruler of the underworld. He represents a more positive aspect of the god who presides over the afterlife, in contrast to Hades.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
