      "headline": "Association with Wealth",
      "text": "Pluto was frequently conflated with Ploûtos, the Greek god of wealth, due to the association of mineral wealth found underground and the chthonic nature of Pluto ruling the deep earth.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Role in the Eleusinian Mysteries",
      "text": "The name Ploutōn came into widespread usage with the Eleusinian Mysteries, where Pluto was venerated as both a stern ruler and a loving husband to Persephone.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pluto and Persephone",
      "text": "Pluto and Persephone were invoked together in religious inscriptions as Plouton and Kore, respectively. They were seen as a couple receiving souls in the afterlife.",
      "date": "-0500"
    }
  ]
}

