    {
      "headline": "Formulation of the Categorical Imperative",
      "text": "The categorical imperative is best known in its original formulation: 'Act only according to that maxim whereby you can at the same time will that it should become a universal law.' This formulation emphasizes the universality and necessity of moral laws.",
      "date": "1785"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Moral Philosophy",
      "text": "Since its introduction, the categorical imperative has had a profound influence on moral philosophy, shaping discussions on ethics and morality by emphasizing duty and the universality of moral laws.",
      "date": "1785"
    }
  ]
}

