      "headline": "Development of Sodium Thiopental",
      "text": "Sodium thiopental was developed in the 1930s by Ernest H. Volwiler and Donalee L. Tabern at Abbott Laboratories. It was introduced as a rapid-onset short-acting barbiturate general anesthetic.",
      "date": "1930"
