      "headline": "Siege and Battle of the Alamo",
      "text": "The Battle of the Alamo took place from February 23 to March 6, 1836, during the Texas Revolution. The battle ended with the defeat of the Texan defenders by the Mexican army led by General Antonio López de Santa Anna.",
      "date": "1836-03-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Texas Independence",
      "text": "Following the Battle of the Alamo, the Texas Revolution continued, leading to Texas gaining independence from Mexico later in 1836.",
      "date": "1836"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Preservation Efforts Begin",
      "text": "In the late 19th century, efforts to preserve the Alamo began, recognizing its historical significance.",
      "date": "1880"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alamo Becomes a Museum",
      "text": "The Alamo was officially designated as a museum in the early 20th century, allowing visitors to learn about its history.",
      "date": "1905"
