      "headline": "Establishment of Fushimi Inari-taisha",
      "text": "Fushimi Inari-taisha was established in 711 AD on the Inariyama hill in southwestern Kyoto. It was originally located in the area of Fushimi-ku, Kyoto, Japan.",
      "date": "0711"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Relocation of the Shrine",
      "text": "In 816 AD, the shrine was relocated to its present location at the request of the monk Kūkai.",
      "date": "0816"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reconstruction of the Main Shrine",
      "text": "In 1499, the main shrine structure was rebuilt. This reconstruction is the basis for the current main shrine building.",
      "date": "1499"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Construction of the Senbon Torii",
      "text": "The famous Senbon Torii, or 'thousands of torii gates', were donated by individuals and businesses over the years, with the practice becoming popular in the Edo period (1603-1868).",
      "date": "1603"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Designation as an Important Cultural Property",
      "text": "In 1975, Fushimi Inari-taisha was designated as an Important Cultural Property by the Japanese government.",
      "date": "1975"
    }
  ]
}

