      "headline": "Refusal of Kingship",
      "text": "After his victory, the Israelites asked Gideon to rule over them, but he refused, saying that the Lord would rule over Israel. This event is detailed in Judges 8:22-23.",
      "date": "-1200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the Ephod",
      "text": "Gideon made an ephod from the gold taken as spoils of war, which became a snare to him and his family, as it led the Israelites into idolatry. This is described in Judges 8:24-27.",
      "date": "-1200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gideon's Death",
      "text": "Gideon died at a good old age and was buried in the tomb of his father Joash in Ophrah of the Abiezrites. His death marked the beginning of a period of idolatry among the Israelites.",
      "date": "-1150"
    }
  ]
}

