      "text": "As some unicorns grew even larger, new terms like 'decacorn' (for companies valued at over $10 billion) and 'hectocorn' (for those valued at over $100 billion) were introduced to describe these exceptionally high-valued startups.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Expansion of Unicorns",
      "text": "By 2017, unicorns were no longer confined to the United States, with significant numbers emerging in China, India, and Europe, indicating a global expansion of high-valued startups.",
