      "headline": "First Polynesian Settlement",
      "text": "The first Polynesian settlers arrived in Aotearoa, now known as New Zealand, around 1250-1300 CE. These settlers are the ancestors of the Māori people.",
      "date": "1250"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Māori Culture Flourishes",
      "text": "Between 1300 and 1800, Māori culture developed and flourished in Aotearoa, with distinct tribal groups and a rich tradition of oral history, art, and navigation.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dutch Explorer Abel Tasman Arrives",
      "text": "In December 1642, Dutch explorer Abel Tasman became the first European to sight New Zealand. He anchored at the northern end of the South Island.",
      "date": "1642-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Captain James Cook's First Voyage",
      "text": "In 1769, British explorer Captain James Cook arrived in New Zealand on his first voyage, mapping the coastline and establishing contact with Māori.",
