    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Large Denominations",
      "text": "Large denominations of United States currency greater than $100 were first introduced in the late 19th century to facilitate large financial transactions.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Series of 1861",
      "text": "The first $500 bill was issued as part of the Series of 1861, during the American Civil War, to help finance the war effort.",
