      "headline": "Evolutionary Origin",
      "text": "Baleen whales are part of the parvorder Mysticeti in the infraorder Cetacea. They evolved to use keratinaceous baleen plates in their mouths to sieve planktonic creatures from the water.",
      "date": "-34000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Classification",
      "text": "Mysticeti comprises the families Balaenidae, Balaenopteridae (rorquals), Eschrichtiidae, and Cetotheriidae.",
