      "headline": "Babri Masjid Construction",
      "text": "In 1528, the Babri Masjid was constructed by Mir Baqi, a general of the Mughal emperor Babur, on the site that is believed by some to be the birthplace of Rama.",
      "date": "1528"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Recorded Communal Clashes",
      "text": "In 1853, the first recorded communal clashes over the site occurred between Hindus and Muslims.",
      "date": "1853"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Administration Divides the Site",
      "text": "In 1859, the British administration erected a fence to divide the mosque from the Hindu temple, allowing the inner court to be used by Muslims and the outer court by Hindus.",
      "date": "1859"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Idols Placed Inside Mosque",
      "text": "On the night of December 22-23, 1949, idols of Rama were placed inside the mosque, leading to both Hindu and Muslim protests.",
      "date": "1949-12-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Court Orders Site Locked",
      "text": "In 1950, the civil court ordered the site to be locked, allowing only a Hindu priest to perform rituals inside.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Unlocking of the Site",
      "text": "In 1986, a district judge ordered the gates of the disputed site to be unlocked, allowing Hindus to worship there.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of VHP and BJP Campaign",
      "text": "In the late 1980s, the Vishva Hindu Parishad (VHP) and Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) began a campaign to construct a temple at the site.",
      "date": "1980s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Demolition of Babri Masjid",
      "text": "On December 6, 1992, the Babri Masjid was demolished by a large group of activists, leading to widespread riots across India.",
      "date": "1992-12-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Archaeological Survey of India Report",
      "text": "In 2003, the Archaeological Survey of India conducted an excavation and reported evidence of a temple-like structure beneath the mosque site.",
      "date": "2003"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Allahabad High Court Verdict",
      "text": "On September 30, 2010, the Allahabad High Court ruled that the 2.77 acres of disputed land be divided into three parts among Hindus, Muslims, and the Nirmohi Akhara.",
      "date": "2010-09-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Supreme Court Verdict",
      "text": "On November 9, 2019, the Supreme Court of India awarded the entire disputed land to the Hindu parties for the construction of a temple and ordered the government to provide an alternative site to Muslims for a mosque.",
      "date": "2019-11-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Foundation Stone Laying Ceremony",
      "text": "On August 5, 2020, the foundation stone for the Ram Temple was laid by Prime Minister Narendra Modi in a grand ceremony.",
