      "text": "A total solar eclipse will occur on August 12, 2026. During this event, the Moon will pass between Earth and the Sun, completely obscuring the Sun's image for viewers in the path of totality. The eclipse will have a magnitude of 1.0386, and will occur approximately 2.2 days after the Moon reaches perigee, making its apparent diameter larger than the Sun's.",
