      "text": "The concept of using sound to detect objects underwater dates back to the late 15th century when Leonardo da Vinci proposed using a tube to listen for ships.",
      "date": "1490"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Practical Sonar Device",
      "text": "In 1915, Paul Langevin and Constantin Chilowski developed the first practical sonar device, which used the piezoelectric effect to detect submarines.",
