    {
      "headline": "Advisory Panel Report",
      "text": "In 1980, a panel of scientific experts, known as the Ruina Panel, was convened to review the data from the Vela incident. The panel concluded that the data was not definitive enough to confirm a nuclear explosion, suggesting that the flash could have been caused by a natural phenomenon or a satellite malfunction.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ongoing Speculation and Research",
      "text": "Over the years, independent researchers and analysts have continued to study the Vela incident. Many have concluded that the double flash was indeed the result of a nuclear test, citing circumstantial evidence and geopolitical context.",
