    {
      "headline": "Introduction of ICMP",
      "text": "The Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) was introduced as part of the original Internet Protocol suite, which was developed in the late 1970s. ICMP is used by network devices to send error messages and operational information.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of ICMP in RFC 777",
      "text": "ICMP was first specified in RFC 777, published in April 1981. This document outlined the initial design and purpose of ICMP within the Internet Protocol suite.",
      "date": "1981-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ICMP Specification in RFC 792",
      "text": "The formal specification of ICMP was published in RFC 792 in September 1981. This document provided detailed descriptions of ICMP message types and their functions.",
      "date": "1981-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ICMPv6 Specification",
      "text": "With the development of IPv6, ICMPv6 was introduced as part of the new protocol suite. ICMPv6 was specified in RFC 2463, published in December 1998, to handle error messages and operational information for IPv6 networks.",
      "date": "1998-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "ICMPv6 Updated in RFC 4443",
      "text": "RFC 4443, published in March 2006, updated the ICMPv6 specification to address issues and improve functionality in IPv6 networks.",
      "date": "2006-03"
    }
  ]
