      "headline": "Carboniferous Period",
      "text": "The Carboniferous period, starting around 358.9 million years ago, is known for the extensive forests of vascular plants that led to the formation of vast coal deposits.",
      "date": "-0358.9"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Permian Period",
      "text": "The Permian period, beginning approximately 298.9 million years ago, ended with the largest mass extinction in Earth's history, wiping out a significant percentage of marine and terrestrial species.",
      "date": "-0298.9"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Triassic Period",
      "text": "Starting around 251.9 million years ago, the Triassic period saw the rise of dinosaurs and the first mammals.",
      "date": "-0251.9"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Jurassic Period",
      "text": "The Jurassic period, beginning approximately 201.3 million years ago, is known for the dominance of dinosaurs and the appearance of the first birds.",
      "date": "-0201.3"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cretaceous Period",
      "text": "Starting around 145 million years ago, the Cretaceous period ended with the mass extinction event that led to the demise of the dinosaurs.",
