      "headline": "Formation of the White Cliffs of Dover",
      "text": "The White Cliffs of Dover were formed during the Late Cretaceous period, approximately 70 to 100 million years ago, due to the accumulation of coccoliths, the calcite plates of micro-organisms, which settled on the sea floor and eventually formed chalk.",
      "date": "-010000000"
