      "text": "In April 1917, Marcel Duchamp created Fountain, a readymade sculpture consisting of a porcelain urinal signed 'R. Mutt'. Duchamp submitted it for the inaugural exhibition of the Society of Independent Artists in New York.",
      "date": "1917-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Submission to the Society of Independent Artists",
      "text": "Fountain was submitted to the Society of Independent Artists' exhibition in April 1917. Despite the Society's rules that all works would be accepted from artists who paid the fee, Fountain was never placed in the show area.",
      "date": "1917-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Photograph by Alfred Stieglitz",
      "text": "After its removal from the exhibition, Fountain was photographed by Alfred Stieglitz at his studio. The photograph was later published in the Dada journal The Blind Man.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication in The Blind Man",
      "text": "The photograph of Fountain taken by Alfred Stieglitz was published in the Dada journal The Blind Man in 1917, bringing attention to Duchamp's work.",
      "date": "1917"
