      "headline": "Release of Who's Next",
      "text": "Who's Next, the fifth studio album by the English rock band the Who, was released on 2 August 1971 by Track Records in the United Kingdom and Decca Records in the United States.",
      "date": "1971-08-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development from Lifehouse Project",
      "text": "Who's Next developed from the aborted Lifehouse project, a multi-media rock opera conceived by the group's guitarist Pete Townshend as a follow-up to the band's 1969 album Tommy. The project was cancelled due to its complexity and conflicts with Kit Lambert, the band's manager.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Salvaging of Lifehouse Songs",
      "text": "The group salvaged some of the songs from the Lifehouse project, without the connecting story elements, to release as their next album, Who's Next. Eight of the nine songs on the album were from Lifehouse, with the exception of 'My Wife' penned by John Entwistle.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of Remaining Lifehouse Tracks",
      "text": "Ultimately, the remaining Lifehouse tracks would all be released on other albums throughout the next decade.",
      "date": "1970s"
    }
  ]
}

