      "headline": "Design and Development",
      "text": "The Lewis gun was designed by U.S. Army Colonel Isaac Newton Lewis in 1911. Despite being designed in the United States, it was not adopted by the U.S. military.",
      "date": "1911"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Production in the United Kingdom",
      "text": "The design was finalized and mass-produced in the United Kingdom. The Birmingham Small Arms Company (BSA) was one of the main manufacturers.",
