      "text": "The Lewis gun was adopted by the British Army and used extensively during World War I. It became a standard issue for British troops.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Use in World War I",
      "text": "The Lewis gun was widely used by troops of the British Empire during World War I. It was known for its distinctive barrel cooling shroud and top-mounted pan magazine.",
      "date": "1914-1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Aircraft Machine Gun",
      "text": "The Lewis gun was adapted for use as an aircraft machine gun during World War I, often with the cooling shroud removed for better air flow cooling.",
      "date": "1914-1918"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Interwar Period Usage",
      "text": "The Lewis gun continued to be used by various military forces during the interwar period, including in colonial conflicts and by police forces.",
      "date": "1919-1938"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Use in World War II",
      "text": "The Lewis gun saw continued use during World War II, particularly in the early years of the war, by British and Commonwealth forces.",
      "date": "1939-1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service in the Korean War",
      "text": "The Lewis gun was used until the end of the Korean War, marking the end of its service life in major conflicts.",
      "date": "1950-1953"
    }
  ]
}

