      "text": "In 1781, a devastating smallpox epidemic swept through the Blackfoot Confederacy, drastically reducing their population and impacting their societal structure.",
      "date": "1781"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Signing of Treaty 7",
      "text": "On September 22, 1877, representatives of the Blackfoot Confederacy signed Treaty 7 with the Canadian government, ceding large portions of their territory in exchange for reserves and other promises.",
      "date": "1877-09-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Reserves",
      "text": "Following the signing of Treaty 7, the Blackfoot Confederacy was relocated to reserves in Canada, significantly altering their traditional way of life and land use.",
      "date": "1880"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Blackfeet Indian Reservation",
      "text": "In 1896, the Blackfeet Indian Reservation was established in Montana, USA, for the Southern Piikani, marking a significant change in their living conditions and governance.",
      "date": "1896"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Revival Efforts",
