      "headline": "Discovery of Ozone Depletion",
      "text": "In 1974, scientists Mario Molina and F. Sherwood Rowland published a paper suggesting that CFCs were contributing to the depletion of the ozone layer.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Montreal Protocol",
      "text": "The Montreal Protocol, an international treaty to phase out the production and consumption of ozone-depleting substances including CFCs, was signed in 1987.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "CFC Production Phase-Out",
      "text": "By 1996, developed countries had largely phased out the production of CFCs under the terms of the Montreal Protocol.",
      "date": "1996"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Complete Phase-Out of CFCs",
      "text": "By 2010, the production and consumption of CFCs were completely phased out in developing countries as per the Montreal Protocol.",
