      "headline": "Communist Coup",
      "text": "In February 1948, the Communist Party of Czechoslovakia, with Soviet backing, seized control of the government in a coup d'état, marking the beginning of the Czechoslovak Socialist Republic.",
      "date": "1948-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitution of 1948",
      "text": "On May 9, 1948, a new constitution was adopted, which formalized the country's status as a people's democracy and established the framework for communist rule.",
      "date": "1948-05-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Name Change to Czechoslovak Socialist Republic",
      "text": "In 1960, the country's name was officially changed to the Czechoslovak Socialist Republic, reflecting its socialist orientation.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prague Spring",
      "text": "In 1968, a period of political liberalization known as the Prague Spring occurred, led by Alexander Dubček, which sought to create 'socialism with a human face.'",
      "date": "1968"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Warsaw Pact Invasion",
      "text": "On August 20-21, 1968, Warsaw Pact troops invaded Czechoslovakia to halt the reforms of the Prague Spring, leading to the end of the liberalization efforts.",
      "date": "1968-08-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Normalization Period",
      "text": "Following the invasion, a period known as 'Normalization' began, characterized by the restoration of a strict communist regime and suppression of dissent.",
      "date": "1969"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Velvet Revolution",
      "text": "In November 1989, the Velvet Revolution, a non-violent transition of power, led to the end of communist rule in Czechoslovakia.",
      "date": "1989-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution of the Czechoslovak Socialist Republic",
      "text": "On December 29, 1989, Václav Havel was elected president, marking the official end of the Czechoslovak Socialist Republic and the beginning of a democratic government.",
      "date": "1989-12-29"
    }
  ]
}

