      "headline": "Isolation of Adenoviruses",
      "text": "Adenoviruses were first isolated from human adenoids in 1953. This discovery marked the identification of a new group of viruses that would become significant in both medical and scientific research.",
      "date": "1953"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Classification of Adenoviridae",
      "text": "Following their discovery, adenoviruses were classified into the family Adenoviridae. This classification helped in understanding their structure, genetic makeup, and the diseases they cause.",
      "date": "1950s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Adenovirus Vectors",
      "text": "In the late 20th century, adenoviruses began to be used as vectors in gene therapy and vaccine development due to their ability to deliver genetic material into host cells.",
      "date": "1980s-1990s"
    },
