{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "headline": "Initial Development of POSIX",
      "text": "In the early 1980s, the IEEE began developing a standard to ensure compatibility between different Unix systems. This effort was aimed at creating a unified standard for operating systems to follow, which would later become known as POSIX.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.1 Standard Published",
      "text": "In 1988, the first version of the POSIX standard, known as POSIX.1, was published. This standard defined a core set of application programming interfaces (APIs) for Unix-based systems.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.2 Standard Published",
      "text": "In 1992, the POSIX.2 standard was published, which specified command-line shell and utility interfaces for Unix-based systems, further enhancing software compatibility.",
      "date": "1992"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX Becomes an International Standard",
      "text": "In 1990, POSIX was adopted as an international standard by the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) and the International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC), under the name ISO/IEC 9945.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.1b Real-Time Extensions",
      "text": "In 1993, the POSIX.1b standard was introduced, adding real-time extensions to the original POSIX.1 standard, allowing for better support of real-time computing.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.1c Threads Extension",
      "text": "In 1995, the POSIX.1c standard was published, introducing support for multi-threading, which allowed for concurrent execution of multiple threads within a single process.",
      "date": "1995"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Single UNIX Specification Incorporation",
      "text": "In 1997, the Single UNIX Specification was incorporated into the POSIX standard, aligning the two standards and further promoting compatibility across Unix systems.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.1-2001 Standard",
      "text": "In 2001, a major revision of the POSIX standard was released, known as POSIX.1-2001. This revision included updates and consolidations of previous standards, enhancing system and application compatibility.",
      "date": "2001"
    },
    {
      "headline": "POSIX.1-2008 Standard",
      "text": "In 2008, another major revision of the POSIX standard was released, known as POSIX.1-2008. This version included further updates and refinements to the existing standards.",
      "date": "2008"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
