      "headline": "Introduction of Plug-in Hybrid Concept",
      "text": "The concept of plug-in hybrid vehicles (PHEVs) began to gain attention as a potential solution for reducing emissions and improving fuel efficiency by combining electric and traditional combustion engine technologies.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Production Plug-in Hybrid",
      "text": "In 2008, the first production plug-in hybrid vehicle, the BYD F3DM, was launched in China. It marked a significant milestone in the automotive industry by offering a vehicle that could be charged from an external power source.",
