      "headline": "Discovery of the Photovoltaic Effect",
      "text": "In 1839, French physicist Alexandre Edmond Becquerel discovered the photovoltaic effect, which is the principle behind solar cells. He found that certain materials would produce small amounts of electric current when exposed to light.",
      "date": "1839"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Practical Solar Cell",
      "text": "In 1954, Bell Labs produced the first practical photovoltaic cell. This silicon solar cell was capable of converting sunlight into electricity with an efficiency of about 6%.",
      "date": "1954"
