      "date": "1865-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Terms of Surrender",
      "text": "The terms of surrender were generous: Confederate soldiers were allowed to return home with their personal possessions, horses, and sidearms. This was agreed upon on April 9, 1865, at the McLean House in Appomattox Court House, Virginia.",
      "date": "1865-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact of the Surrender",
      "text": "The surrender at Appomattox Court House on April 9, 1865, marked the beginning of the end of the American Civil War. It led to the surrender of other Confederate armies and the eventual restoration of the Union.",
