    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence Movement",
      "text": "Michoacán played a significant role in the Mexican War of Independence, which began in 1810. José María Morelos, a native of the region, was a key leader in the movement.",
      "date": "1810"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Statehood",
      "text": "Michoacán became a state of the newly independent Mexico in 1824, following the end of Spanish rule.",
      "date": "1824"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Renaming of Morelia",
      "text": "In 1828, the city of Valladolid was renamed Morelia in honor of José María Morelos.",
      "date": "1828"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cristero War",
      "text": "During the Cristero War (1926-1929), Michoacán was one of the central regions of conflict between the Mexican government and Catholic rebels.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Era",
      "text": "In recent decades, Michoacán has faced challenges related to drug trafficking and violence, impacting its social and economic development.",
