    {
      "headline": "Emergence of Humanist Sans-serifs",
      "text": "Humanist sans-serif typefaces, which are inspired by traditional serif typefaces and calligraphy, became popular in the late 20th century. These typefaces, such as Gill Sans and Frutiger, offer a more organic and readable appearance.",
      "date": "1900s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Digital Era and Sans-serif Typefaces",
      "text": "With the advent of digital typography in the late 20th and early 21st centuries, sans-serif typefaces became even more prevalent due to their readability on screens and adaptability to various digital formats.",
      "date": "1990s-2000s"
