      "text": "Constructed in the 9th century, Borobudur in Indonesia is one of the largest and most famous Buddhist stupas in the world. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
      "date": "0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Stupas in Tibet",
      "text": "Stupas became prominent in Tibet by the 7th century, where they were known as chortens and incorporated into Tibetan Buddhist practices.",
