      "text": "Yuan Shikai, the de facto dictator of China, died on June 6, 1916. His death marked the beginning of the Warlord Era as it created a power vacuum in China.",
      "date": "1916-06-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Beginning of the Warlord Era",
      "text": "Following Yuan Shikai's death, China entered the Warlord Era, characterized by the fragmentation of power among military cliques and regional factions.",
      "date": "1916"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Anhui and Zhili Cliques",
      "text": "In the aftermath of Yuan's death, the Beiyang Army split into various factions, including the Anhui and Zhili cliques, which became prominent power players during the Warlord Era.",
      "date": "1916"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitution Protection Movement",
      "text": "In 1917, Sun Yat-sen launched the Constitution Protection Movement in Guangzhou to challenge the legitimacy of the Beiyang government in Beijing.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Zhili-Anhui War",
      "text": "The Zhili-Anhui War occurred in July 1920, resulting in the defeat of the Anhui clique by the Zhili clique.",
      "date": "1920-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Zhili-Fengtian War",
      "text": "The First Zhili-Fengtian War took place in 1922, with the Zhili clique defeating the Fengtian clique.",
      "date": "1922"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Zhili-Fengtian War",
      "text": "In 1924, the Second Zhili-Fengtian War occurred, leading to the defeat of the Zhili clique by the Fengtian clique.",
      "date": "1924"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Northern Expedition",
      "text": "The Northern Expedition, launched by the Nationalist Kuomintang (KMT) in 1926, aimed to unify China by defeating the warlords.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Warlord Era",
      "text": "The Warlord Era effectively ended in 1928 when the Nationalist government, led by Chiang Kai-shek, established control over most of China after the Northern Expedition.",
      "date": "1928"
    }
  ]
}

