      "headline": "Beginning of the Late Middle Ages",
      "text": "The Late Middle Ages is generally considered to have begun around the year 1300, following the High Middle Ages.",
      "date": "1300"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Great Famine",
      "text": "The Great Famine of 1315-1317 was a period of mass starvation and disease in Europe, caused by a series of poor harvests.",
      "date": "1315"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Black Death",
      "text": "The Black Death, one of the deadliest pandemics in human history, reached Europe in 1347 and lasted until 1351, killing an estimated 25-30 million people.",
      "date": "1347"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Hundred Years' War Begins",
      "text": "The Hundred Years' War between England and France began in 1337, lasting until 1453, marked by a series of conflicts over territorial claims.",
      "date": "1337"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Battle of Agincourt",
      "text": "The Battle of Agincourt took place on October 25, 1415, where the English army, led by King Henry V, achieved a decisive victory against the French.",
      "date": "1415-10-25"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joan of Arc's Campaign",
      "text": "In 1429, Joan of Arc led the French army to several important victories during the Hundred Years' War, including the Siege of Orléans.",
      "date": "1429"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Fall of Constantinople",
      "text": "The Fall of Constantinople on May 29, 1453, marked the end of the Byzantine Empire and is often considered the end of the Middle Ages.",
      "date": "1453-05-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The Printing Press Invented",
      "text": "Johannes Gutenberg invented the movable-type printing press around 1440, revolutionizing the spread of information in Europe.",
      "date": "1440"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Hundred Years' War",
      "text": "The Hundred Years' War ended in 1453 with the French recapture of Bordeaux, marking the end of English territorial claims in France.",
      "date": "1453"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The War of the Roses Begins",
      "text": "The War of the Roses, a series of civil wars for control of the throne of England, began in 1455 between the houses of Lancaster and York.",
      "date": "1455"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Christopher Columbus's First Voyage",
      "text": "In 1492, Christopher Columbus embarked on his first voyage across the Atlantic Ocean, leading to the European discovery of the Americas.",
      "date": "1492"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Reconquista",
      "text": "The Reconquista ended in 1492 with the fall of Granada, the last Muslim stronghold in Spain, marking the completion of the Christian reconquest of the Iberian Peninsula.",
      "date": "1492"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Late Middle Ages",
      "text": "The Late Middle Ages is generally considered to have ended around the year 1500, transitioning into the early modern period.",
      "date": "1500"
    }
  ]
}

