      "headline": "January 6 United States Capitol Attack",
      "text": "On January 6, 2021, supporters of Donald Trump attacked the U.S. Capitol building, disrupting the joint session of Congress assembled to count electoral votes to formalize Biden's victory in the 2020 United States presidential election.",
      "date": "2021-01-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Arrests",
      "text": "The first arrests related to the Capitol attack began shortly after January 6, 2021, as law enforcement identified and apprehended individuals involved in the breach.",
      "date": "2021-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Guilty Plea",
      "text": "On April 16, 2021, Jon Schaffer, a member of the Oath Keepers, became the first person to plead guilty to charges related to the Capitol attack.",
      "date": "2021-04-16"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Sentencing",
      "text": "On July 19, 2021, Paul Hodgkins became the first person to be sentenced for his role in the Capitol attack, receiving an eight-month prison sentence.",
      "date": "2021-07-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Felony Sentence",
      "text": "On November 10, 2021, Scott Fairlamb was sentenced to 41 months in prison, marking the first felony sentence related to the Capitol attack.",
      "date": "2021-11-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Jury Trial Conviction",
      "text": "On March 8, 2022, Guy Reffitt was convicted on all counts in the first jury trial related to the Capitol attack.",
      "date": "2022-03-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Seditious Conspiracy Convictions",
      "text": "On November 29, 2022, Stewart Rhodes and Kelly Meggs were found guilty of seditious conspiracy, marking the first convictions for this charge related to the Capitol attack.",
      "date": "2022-11-29"
    }
  ]
}

