      "headline": "Establishment of the Ryukyu Kingdom",
      "text": "In 1429, the Ryukyu Kingdom was established, unifying the islands under the rule of King Shō Hashi, who became the first king of the unified Ryukyu Kingdom.",
      "date": "1429"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ryukyu Kingdom's Tributary Relationship with China",
      "text": "The Ryukyu Kingdom established a tributary relationship with the Ming Dynasty of China, which began in 1372 and continued for several centuries, facilitating trade and cultural exchange.",
      "date": "1372"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Satsuma Domain's Invasion",
      "text": "In 1609, the Satsuma Domain of Japan invaded the Ryukyu Kingdom, leading to its subjugation and the beginning of a dual subordination to both China and Japan.",
      "date": "1609"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by Japan",
      "text": "In 1879, the Ryukyu Kingdom was formally annexed by Japan, becoming Okinawa Prefecture, and marking the end of the Ryukyu Kingdom.",
      "date": "1879"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Okinawa",
      "text": "In 1945, during World War II, the Battle of Okinawa took place, resulting in significant casualties and destruction on the islands.",
