      "headline": "Chrétien de Troyes' Arthurian Romances",
      "text": "In the late 12th century, Chrétien de Troyes, a French poet, wrote several Arthurian romances, including Lancelot, Perceval, and Yvain. These works expanded the Arthurian legends and introduced new characters and themes.",
      "date": "1190"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Geoffrey of Monmouth",
      "text": "Geoffrey of Monmouth died in 1155. His works, particularly the Historia Regum Britanniae, left a lasting impact on the Matter of Britain and the development of Arthurian legends.",
      "date": "1155"
    }
  ]
}

