      "text": "Sergey Alexandrovich Yesenin was born on October 3, 1895, in Konstantinovo, Ryazan Governorate, Russian Empire.",
      "date": "1895-10-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Publication",
      "text": "In 1914, Yesenin's first poem was published in a children's magazine, marking the beginning of his literary career.",
      "date": "1914"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Petrograd",
      "text": "In 1915, Yesenin moved to Petrograd (now Saint Petersburg) where he met prominent Russian poets like Alexander Blok and became part of the literary scene.",
      "date": "1915"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Zinaida Raikh",
      "text": "Yesenin married Zinaida Raikh in 1917, and they had two children together before divorcing in 1921.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Radunitsa'",
      "text": "In 1916, Yesenin published his first book of poems, 'Radunitsa', which gained him significant recognition.",
      "date": "1916"
