      "headline": "Marriage to Isadora Duncan",
      "text": "In 1922, Yesenin married the famous American dancer Isadora Duncan. The marriage attracted significant media attention.",
      "date": "1922"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Tour of Europe and the United States",
      "text": "Between 1922 and 1923, Yesenin toured Europe and the United States with Isadora Duncan, during which he wrote several poems.",
      "date": "1922"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to Russia",
      "text": "Yesenin returned to Russia in 1923 after his tour with Isadora Duncan, and their marriage ended shortly after.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Confessions of a Hooligan'",
      "text": "In 1921, Yesenin published 'Confessions of a Hooligan', a collection that reflected his rebellious and bohemian lifestyle.",
      "date": "1921"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Sergey Yesenin",
      "text": "Sergey Yesenin died on December 28, 1925, in the Angleterre Hotel in Leningrad (now Saint Petersburg), under circumstances that led to much speculation.",
