      "text": "In 1861, James Clerk Maxwell published a set of equations that describe the behavior of both electric and magnetic fields, unifying the concepts of electricity and magnetism.",
      "date": "1861"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Electrostatic Generators",
      "text": "Throughout the 18th and 19th centuries, various electrostatic generators were developed, including the Wimshurst machine and the Van de Graaff generator, which are used to produce high voltages.",
      "date": "1800"
