      "text": "The Battle of Zama was fought in 202 BC in what is now Tunisia. It was a decisive battle of the Second Punic War between a Roman army commanded by Scipio Africanus and a Carthaginian army commanded by Hannibal. The Roman army, although outnumbered, was stronger in cavalry and successfully defeated the Carthaginians, who fielded either 40,000 or 50,000 troops and 80 war elephants.",
      "date": "-0202"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Carthaginian Defeat and Capitulation",
      "text": "Following their defeat at the Battle of Zama in 202 BC, the Carthaginians were forced to capitulate. This defeat marked the end of the Second Punic War, with Rome emerging as the dominant power in the western Mediterranean.",
      "date": "-0202"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hannibal's Exile",
      "text": "After the defeat at the Battle of Zama in 202 BC, Hannibal was forced into exile. He fled Carthage to avoid Roman retribution and spent the rest of his life in various foreign courts.",
      "date": "-0202"
    }
  ]
}

