      "headline": "Formation of the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL)",
      "text": "In April 2013, the Islamic State of Iraq (ISI) announced its expansion into Syria and rebranded itself as the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL).",
      "date": "2013-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture of Raqqa",
      "text": "In March 2013, ISIL captured the city of Raqqa in Syria, making it the de facto capital of their self-proclaimed caliphate.",
      "date": "2013-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declaration of the Caliphate",
      "text": "On June 29, 2014, ISIL declared the establishment of a caliphate, renaming itself the Islamic State (IS) and declaring Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi as its caliph.",
      "date": "2014-06-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture of Mosul",
      "text": "In June 2014, IS captured Mosul, Iraq's second-largest city, marking a significant expansion of their territory.",
      "date": "2014-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Kobani",
      "text": "From September 2014 to January 2015, IS forces besieged the Syrian town of Kobani but were eventually repelled by Kurdish forces with international support.",
      "date": "2014-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Tikrit",
      "text": "In March 2015, IS lost control of the city of Tikrit in Iraq after a major offensive by Iraqi forces and allied militias.",
      "date": "2015-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Ramadi",
      "text": "In December 2015, Iraqi forces recaptured the city of Ramadi from IS, marking a significant defeat for the group.",
      "date": "2015-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Fallujah",
      "text": "In June 2016, Iraqi forces recaptured Fallujah from IS, further reducing their territorial control in Iraq.",
      "date": "2016-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Mosul",
      "text": "From October 2016 to July 2017, Iraqi forces, with international support, conducted a major offensive to recapture Mosul from IS, which was successful.",
      "date": "2016-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Raqqa",
      "text": "In October 2017, the Syrian Democratic Forces, with international support, recaptured Raqqa from IS, effectively ending their control over their self-proclaimed capital.",
      "date": "2017-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Baghouz",
      "text": "In March 2019, IS lost its last significant stronghold in Syria, the town of Baghouz, to the Syrian Democratic Forces.",
      "date": "2019-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "IS Control in Mali",
      "text": "As of 2023, large swathes of Mali have fallen under IS control, marking a significant territorial presence in West Africa.",
      "date": "2023"
