      "text": "Norway claimed Queen Maud Land in Antarctica on January 14, 1939.",
      "date": "1939-01-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chilean Antarctic Territory",
      "text": "Chile made its claim to Antarctic territory in 1940, overlapping with the British and Argentine claims.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Argentine Antarctic Claim",
      "text": "Argentina formally claimed its Antarctic territory in 1943, which overlaps with both the British and Chilean claims.",
      "date": "1943"
    },
    {
      "headline": "French Claim on Adélie Land",
      "text": "France claimed Adélie Land in Antarctica in 1924, but it was formally recognized in 1938.",
      "date": "1938"
    },
    {
      "headline": "New Zealand's Ross Dependency",
      "text": "New Zealand claimed the Ross Dependency in 1923, which was administered by New Zealand on behalf of the United Kingdom.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Antarctic Treaty System",
      "text": "The Antarctic Treaty was signed on December 1, 1959, and entered into force on June 23, 1961. It set aside territorial claims and established Antarctica as a scientific preserve.",
      "date": "1959-12-01"
    }
  ]
