      "text": "Monterey was founded on June 3, 1770, by Father Junípero Serra and explorer Gaspar de Portolá. It was the second permanent settlement established by the Spanish Empire in what is now California.",
      "date": "1770-06-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Monterey Becomes Capital of Alta California",
      "text": "In 1804, Monterey became the capital of Alta California under Spanish rule, a status it maintained under Mexican rule from 1822 to 1846.",
