      "text": "World War I began on July 28, 1914, with Austria-Hungary's declaration of war on Serbia, leading to the mobilization of Russia against Austria-Hungary.",
      "date": "1914-07-28"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Tannenberg",
      "text": "The Battle of Tannenberg took place from August 26 to August 30, 1914. It was a decisive German victory against Russia, with the German Eighth Army encircling and defeating the Russian Second Army.",
      "date": "1914-08-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Battle of the Masurian Lakes",
      "text": "From September 7 to September 14, 1914, the First Battle of the Masurian Lakes occurred, resulting in another German victory that pushed Russian forces out of East Prussia.",
      "date": "1914-09-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gorlice–Tarnów Offensive",
      "text": "The Gorlice–Tarnów Offensive began on May 2, 1915, and marked a major Central Powers victory, leading to the recapture of Galicia from Russian forces.",
      "date": "1915-05-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Great Retreat",
      "text": "The Great Retreat was a strategic withdrawal by Russian forces from Poland and Galicia, beginning in July 1915, following the Gorlice–Tarnów Offensive.",
      "date": "1915-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Brusilov Offensive",
      "text": "The Brusilov Offensive, launched on June 4, 1916, was a major Russian attack against the Austro-Hungarian forces, resulting in significant territorial gains and heavy casualties for the Central Powers.",
      "date": "1916-06-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Romania Enters the War",
      "text": "Romania declared war on Austria-Hungary on August 27, 1916, joining the Allies and opening a new front in the Eastern Theater.",
      "date": "1916-08-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Revolution Begins",
      "text": "The Russian Revolution began in March 1917, leading to significant political upheaval and impacting the Eastern Front as Russian military operations were disrupted.",
      "date": "1917-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Brest-Litovsk",
      "text": "The Treaty of Brest-Litovsk was signed on March 3, 1918, between Soviet Russia and the Central Powers, marking Russia's exit from World War I and ceding significant territories to Germany and Austria-Hungary.",
      "date": "1918-03-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of World War I",
      "text": "World War I ended on November 11, 1918, with the signing of the Armistice of Compiègne, bringing an end to hostilities on the Eastern Front as well.",
