      "text": "Around 14 million years ago, the Middle Miocene Climate Transition occurred, characterized by a global cooling trend and the expansion of Antarctic ice sheets.",
      "date": "-14000000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Late Miocene",
      "text": "The Late Miocene, starting around 11.63 million years ago, saw further cooling and drying of the global climate. This period led to the expansion of savannas and the evolution of many modern plant and animal species.",
      "date": "-11630000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Miocene Epoch",
      "text": "The Miocene Epoch ended approximately 5.333 million years ago, transitioning into the Pliocene Epoch. This period was marked by significant evolutionary changes and the continued development of modern ecosystems.",
      "date": "-5333000"
    }
  ]
}

