      "text": "The first recorded eruption of Mayon Volcano occurred in 1616. This marked the beginning of documented volcanic activity for Mayon.",
      "date": "1616"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Most Violent Eruption",
      "text": "On February 1, 1814, Mayon Volcano erupted violently, resulting in the destruction of the town of Cagsawa and the death of approximately 1,200 people. The eruption is considered the most violent in Mayon's history.",
      "date": "1814-02-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 1897",
      "text": "In June 1897, Mayon erupted again, causing significant damage and loss of life. The eruption lasted for seven days and resulted in the deaths of over 400 people.",
      "date": "1897-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 1984",
      "text": "Mayon erupted on September 23, 1984, prompting the evacuation of thousands of residents. The eruption lasted for two months, but due to timely evacuations, casualties were minimized.",
      "date": "1984-09-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 1993",
      "text": "On February 2, 1993, Mayon erupted again, resulting in the deaths of 77 people. The eruption highlighted the need for improved disaster preparedness and response.",
      "date": "1993-02-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 2006",
      "text": "In July 2006, Mayon Volcano erupted, leading to the evacuation of thousands of residents. The eruption was characterized by lava flows and ash emissions.",
      "date": "2006-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 2009",
      "text": "Mayon erupted on December 14, 2009, prompting the evacuation of over 40,000 residents. The eruption was marked by lava flows and ash plumes.",
      "date": "2009-12-14"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Eruption of 2018",
      "text": "In January 2018, Mayon Volcano erupted, leading to the evacuation of more than 80,000 people. The eruption featured lava fountains and ash plumes, affecting nearby communities.",
      "date": "2018-01"
    }
  ]
}

