      "text": "In 2011, the European Union was granted enhanced rights at the United Nations General Assembly. These rights included the ability to speak in debates, submit proposals and amendments, the right of reply, raise points of order, and circulate documents. This was a significant development as it likened the EU's rights to those of full membership, short of the right to vote.",
