      "headline": "Establishment of the Chagatai Khanate",
      "text": "The Chagatai Khanate was established following the division of the Mongol Empire after the death of Genghis Khan in 1227. It was ruled by Chagatai Khan, the second son of Genghis Khan.",
      "date": "1227"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Chagatai Khan",
      "text": "Chagatai Khan ruled the Chagatai Khanate from its establishment in 1227 until his death in 1242. During his reign, he maintained the Mongol Empire's laws and traditions.",
      "date": "1227-1242"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Chagatai Khan",
      "text": "Chagatai Khan died in 1242, leading to a period of instability and succession disputes within the khanate.",
      "date": "1242"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Alghu Khan",
      "text": "Alghu Khan, a descendant of Chagatai, ruled the khanate from 1260 to 1266, during which he attempted to assert independence from the Great Khan.",
      "date": "1260-1266"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Duwa Khan",
      "text": "Duwa Khan ruled from 1282 to 1307 and was known for his efforts to consolidate power and expand the khanate's influence.",
      "date": "1282-1307"
    },
