    {
      "headline": "Coining of the Term 'BASE Jumping'",
      "text": "In 1981, Carl Boenish coined the term 'BASE jumping' as an acronym for Building, Antenna, Span, and Earth, the four categories of fixed objects from which one can jump.",
      "date": "1981"
    },
