      "headline": "Foundation of the Almohad Movement",
      "text": "The Almohad movement was founded by Ibn Tumart in the early 12th century. He began preaching a return to the original teachings of Islam and gathered a following among the Berber tribes in the Atlas Mountains.",
      "date": "1121"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ibn Tumart Declares Himself Mahdi",
      "text": "In 1121, Ibn Tumart declared himself the Mahdi, a prophesied redeemer of Islam, and began to consolidate power among the Berber tribes.",
      "date": "1121"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ibn Tumart",
      "text": "Ibn Tumart died in 1130, leaving his successor, Abd al-Mu'min, to continue the expansion of the Almohad movement.",
      "date": "1130"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abd al-Mu'min Becomes First Almohad Caliph",
      "text": "In 1130, Abd al-Mu'min became the first Almohad Caliph after the death of Ibn Tumart. He began a series of military campaigns to expand Almohad control.",
      "date": "1130"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conquest of Marrakesh",
      "text": "In 1147, the Almohads captured Marrakesh, the capital of the Almoravid dynasty, marking a significant expansion of their empire.",
      "date": "1147"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Almohad Conquest of Al-Andalus",
      "text": "By 1172, the Almohads had extended their control over most of the Iberian Peninsula, known as Al-Andalus, after defeating the Almoravids.",
      "date": "1172"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Alarcos",
      "text": "In 1195, the Almohads won a significant victory against the Christian kingdoms of the Iberian Peninsula at the Battle of Alarcos.",
      "date": "1195"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa",
      "text": "In 1212, the Almohads suffered a major defeat at the Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa against a coalition of Christian forces, marking the beginning of their decline in the Iberian Peninsula.",
      "date": "1212"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of the Almohad Caliphate",
      "text": "Following the defeat at Las Navas de Tolosa, the Almohad Caliphate began to fragment and lose territories in both North Africa and the Iberian Peninsula.",
      "date": "1212"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Fall of Marrakesh",
      "text": "In 1269, Marrakesh fell to the Marinids, marking the end of the Almohad Caliphate's control over its former territories.",
      "date": "1269"
    }
  ]
}

