      "headline": "Establishment of the Crimean Khanate",
      "text": "The Crimean Khanate was established by Hacı I Giray in 1441. It was regarded as the direct heir to the Golden Horde and to Desht-i-Kipchak.",
      "date": "1441"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alliance with the Ottoman Empire",
      "text": "In 1475, the Crimean Khanate became a vassal state of the Ottoman Empire, which provided military support and protection.",
      "date": "1475"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Mengli I Giray",
      "text": "Mengli I Giray, who reigned from 1466 to 1515, was a significant ruler who solidified the Khanate's power and influence in the region.",
      "date": "1466"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Molodi",
      "text": "In 1572, the Crimean Khanate suffered a significant defeat at the Battle of Molodi against the Tsardom of Russia, which halted its expansion into Russian territories.",
      "date": "1572"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of the Crimean Khanate",
      "text": "Throughout the 17th century, the Crimean Khanate experienced a decline in power due to internal strife and external pressures from neighboring states.",
      "date": "1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annexation by the Russian Empire",
      "text": "In 1783, the Crimean Khanate was annexed by the Russian Empire under Catherine the Great, marking the end of its existence as an independent state.",
      "date": "1783"
    }
  ]
}

