      "headline": "Establishment of the National Assembly",
      "text": "The National Assembly of South Africa was established as part of the new democratic government structure following the end of apartheid. It was formed under the interim Constitution of South Africa, which came into effect on April 27, 1994.",
      "date": "1994-04-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Democratic Elections",
      "text": "The first democratic elections in South Africa were held on April 27, 1994, leading to the formation of the first National Assembly. This marked the end of apartheid and the beginning of a new era in South African politics.",
      "date": "1994-04-27"
    },
