      "headline": "Origin of Martingale Betting System",
      "text": "The martingale betting system originated in 18th-century France. It was popularized as a strategy for a coin-tossing game where the gambler wins the stake if the coin comes up heads and loses if it comes up tails.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Basic Principle of Martingale",
      "text": "The basic principle of the martingale strategy involves doubling the bet after every loss. This ensures that the first win would recover all previous losses and gain a profit equal to the original stake.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Connection to St. Petersburg Paradox",
      "text": "The martingale strategy is an instantiation of the St. Petersburg paradox, which is a classical problem in probability theory and economics.",
      "date": "1700"
    }
  ]
}

