      "text": "The Kingdom of Macedon was established in the 8th century BCE. It became a significant power in the ancient Greek world under the Argead dynasty.",
      "date": "-0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reign of Philip II",
      "text": "Philip II of Macedon reigned from 359 BCE to 336 BCE. He expanded the kingdom and established the League of Corinth, uniting most of Greece under Macedonian hegemony.",
      "date": "-0359"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alexander the Great's Conquests",
      "text": "Alexander the Great, son of Philip II, reigned from 336 BCE to 323 BCE. He created one of the largest empires in history, stretching from Greece to Egypt and into northwest India.",
      "date": "-0336"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Conquest of Macedonia",
      "text": "In 168 BCE, the Roman Republic defeated the Macedonian kingdom in the Battle of Pydna, leading to the establishment of the Roman province of Macedonia in 146 BCE.",
      "date": "-0168"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Byzantine Era",
      "text": "After the division of the Roman Empire, Macedonia became part of the Byzantine Empire. It remained under Byzantine control for several centuries, experiencing periods of prosperity and decline.",
      "date": "0395"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Rule",
      "text": "Macedonia fell under Ottoman rule in the late 14th century, following the Battle of Maritsa in 1371 and the Battle of Kosovo in 1389.",
      "date": "1371"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Greek War of Independence",
      "text": "The Greek War of Independence began in 1821, but Macedonia remained under Ottoman control until the Balkan Wars.",
      "date": "1821"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Balkan Wars",
      "text": "During the Balkan Wars (1912-1913), Greece gained control of most of Macedonia, including the city of Thessaloniki.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Incorporation into Greece",
      "text": "Following the Balkan Wars, the Treaty of Bucharest in 1913 formalized the incorporation of most of Macedonia into Greece.",
      "date": "1913"
    },
    {
      "headline": "World War II Occupation",
      "text": "During World War II, Macedonia was occupied by Axis powers from 1941 to 1944. It was divided among Germany, Italy, and Bulgaria.",
      "date": "1941"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Period",
      "text": "After World War II, Macedonia was restored to Greece. It became a significant region for economic development and cultural heritage.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prespa Agreement",
      "text": "In 2018, Greece and North Macedonia signed the Prespa Agreement, resolving the long-standing name dispute and leading to North Macedonia's accession to NATO.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
}

