    {
      "headline": "Standardization of Mkhedruli Script",
      "text": "By the 11th century, Mkhedruli had become the dominant script for secular writing in Georgia, while Asomtavruli and Nuskhuri continued to be used for religious texts.",
      "date": "1000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Usage of Georgian Scripts",
      "text": "In contemporary times, Mkhedruli is the standard script for the Georgian language, while Asomtavruli and Nuskhuri are used by the Georgian Orthodox Church for religious purposes.",
      "date": "2000"
